   "title": "Fani-Kayode assumes duties as Nigeria’s envoy to South Africa",
   "url": "https://punchng.com/fani-kayode-assumes-duties-as-nigerias-envoy-to-south-africa/",
   "domain": "punchng.com",
   "source": "Punch（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:31:10 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793428270.0,
   "ageDays": 0.0,
   "summary": "Nigeria’s High Commissioner to South Africa, Femi Fani-Kayode, has formally assumed diplomatic duties following the presentation of copies of his Letters of Credence to the South African Department of International Relations and Cooperation. According to him, the presentation marked an important diplomatic milestone and the formal commencement of his duties as Nigeria’s High Commissioner to South Africa, effective October 30.",
   "summary_zh": "尼日利亚驻南非高级专员费米·法尼-卡约德在向南非国际关系与合作部递交国书副本后，正式开始履行外交职责。据他表示，此次递交标志着重要的外交里程碑，也标志着其担任尼日利亚驻南非高级专员的任务正式生效，任职日期为10月30日。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Nigeria’s High Commissioner to South Africa, Femi Fani-Kayode, has formally assumed diplomatic duties following the presentation of copies of his Letters of Credence to the South African Department of International Relations and Cooperation. Fani-Kayode disclosed this in a post on his X handle on Saturday, announcing that he presented the documents to the department’s Deputy Director-General of Public Diplomacy and Acting Chief of State Protocol, Clayson Monyela, on Friday. According to him, the presentation marked an important diplomatic milestone and the formal commencement of his duties as Nigeria’s High Commissioner to South Africa, effective October 30. “Following the presentation, I also met with Ambassador Seboga, Deputy Director-General of DIRCO, in his office, as part of my initial diplomatic engagements with senior South African government officials,” he added. Fani-Kayode said the presentation of the copies of the Letters of Credence would precede the ceremonial presentation of the original documents to South African President Cyril Ramaphosa. “The presentation of copies of my Letters of Credence precedes the ceremonial presentation of my Letters of Credence to His Excellency, President Cyril Ramaphosa of the Republic of South Africa, which will take place in a few days’ time,” he stated. Olugbenga Ige is a journalist at Punch Newspapers with over nine years of professional reporting experience. He is known for his sharp eye for compelling stories and a strong instinct for identifying newsworthy developments. Over the years, Olugbenga has built a reputation for turning leads into clear, engaging, and well-structured reports that resonate with readers. His work reflects deep newsroom experience, editorial judgment, and a commitment to accurate, impactful journalism",
