   "title": "Why are paper ballots used for MLC polls? Explained",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/why-are-paper-ballots-used-for-mlc-polls-explained/article71648197.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:35:53 +0530",
   "_dt": 1793419553.0,
   "ageDays": 0.08,
   "summary": "Polling for MLC seats is done through paper ballots. The Congress’ poll performance evoked a public ridicule from Prime Minister Narendra Modi who took a direct swipe at the party’s long-standing campaigns against Electronic Voting Machines (EVMs) and its persistent demand to return to paper ballots.",
   "summary_zh": "人民院议席投票采用纸质选票。人民院的计票表现引发公众嘲讽，印度总理纳伦德拉·莫迪直接挖苦该党长期反对电子投票机（EVM），以及其坚持要求恢复纸质选票的主张。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Elections were held to 28 seats for Members of Legislative Council (MLC) on October 23. The Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) won 13 of the 28 seats across four states while its NDA alliance partners — Shiv Sena (Eknath Shinde), Janata Dal (United) and Janata Dal (Secular) — won one seat each, taking the coalition’s tally to 16. The Congress won only a single seat in Maharashtra. Polling for MLC seats is done through paper ballots. The Congress’ poll performance evoked a public ridicule from Prime Minister Narendra Modi who took a direct swipe at the party’s long-standing campaigns against Electronic Voting Machines (EVMs) and its persistent demand to return to paper ballots. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
