   "title": "Defense minister says Hegseth dismissed talk of alliance strains as 'fake news'",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/defense/20261030/defense-minister-says-hegseth-dismissed-talk-of-alliance-strains-as-fake-news",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:42:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793338923.0,
   "ageDays": 1.01,
   "summary": "Defense Minister Kang Shin-chul said Friday that U.S. Secretary of War Pete Hegseth had dismissed recent speculation about strains in the Korea-U.S. alliance as “fake news” during their meeting earlier this week. “Secretary Hegseth dismissed all the talk going around as ‘fake news,’” Kang said. “And I agree with him.” “I don’t believe such talk can shake the strength of the Korea-U.S. alliance, nor should it,” he added.",
   "summary_zh": "国防部长姜善焯周五表示，美国战争部长皮特·赫格塞思在本周早些时候举行会谈时，将近期有关韩美关系出现裂痕的猜测斥为“虚假新闻”。姜善焯说：“赫格塞思部长驳斥了所有相关说法，称其是‘虚假新闻’。”“我同意他的看法。”他补充道：“我不认为这类说法能够动摇韩美同盟的牢固关系，也不应该如此。”",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Defense Minister Kang Shin-chul said Friday that U.S. Secretary of War Pete Hegseth had dismissed recent speculation about strains in the Korea-U.S. alliance as “fake news” during their meeting earlier this week. Kang made the remarks to reporters as he arrived at the defense ministry in Seoul after attending the ASEAN Defense Ministers’ Meeting-Plus (ADMM-Plus) in the Philippines. Asked whether the two sides had any disagreements, Kang said there were none. “Secretary Hegseth dismissed all the talk going around as ‘fake news,’” Kang said. “And I agree with him.” “I don’t believe such talk can shake the strength of the Korea-U.S. alliance, nor should it,” he added. Kang and Hegseth held their first face-to-face meeting Wednesday in Cebu, Philippines, on the sidelines of ADMM-Plus. The meeting lasted about 40 minutes, longer than the 15 minutes initially scheduled. Their talks came amid concerns about the state of the alliance, including the postponement of the annual Security Consultative Meeting (SCM), differences over the timeline for transferring wartime operational control (OPCON) and reports of restrictions on intelligence sharing. The two sides agreed to hold another defense ministers’ meeting in Washington in December and postpone the SCM until early next year. Asked whether Washington had agreed to complete the full operational capability (FOC) verification for the OPCON transfer at the next SCM, Kang stopped short of giving a direct answer. “The biggest achievement was that we agreed to work together on the OPCON transfer,” he said. He also declined to confirm whether the U.S. had agreed to Seoul’s proposed 2028 target for the transfer. On reports that Washington had restricted some intelligence sharing with Seoul concerning North Korea, Kang played down the issue, saying it affected only a small portion of military intelligence exchanges. He said the matter was not discussed during Wednesday’s meeting, reiterating that the talks had reaffirmed the strength of the alliance",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
