   "title": "From Stability to Opportunity: Reflections on Nigeria’s Engagement with Asia In Beijing, Central Bank of Nigeria @cenbank Governor Olayemi C",
   "url": "https://x.com/LydiaTeeanaJaja/status/2115501028514857079",
   "snippet": "From Stability to Opportunity: Reflections on Nigeria’s Engagement with Asia\n\nIn Beijing, Central Bank of Nigeria @cenbank Governor Olayemi Cardoso (@olayemicardoso1) led discussions across two major forums aimed at expanding Nigeria’s economic and financial ties with China.\n\nThe first gathering brought together business executives, financial experts and industry stakeholders operating along the Nigeria–China trade corridor. Conversations centred on payment systems, foreign exchange, trade financing and the challenges businesses face when conducting cross-border transactions.\n\nThe second forum, organised in collaboration with ICBC, focused on investment opportunities within Nigeria’s financial markets. Institutional investors, development finance organisations and other market participants examined ways to encourage investment and create a more supportive environment for capital inflows.\n\nCardoso also highlighted the importance of improving remittance services for Nigerians living abroad. The CBN’s focus includes making international transfers more affordable, accessible and efficient, while strengthening the financial links between the diaspora and Nigeria’s domestic economy.\n\nRead More 👇\nhttps://t.co/yy1mTATnKV…\n\n@Dattijo",
   "body": "From Stability to Opportunity: Reflections on Nigeria’s Engagement with Asia\n\nIn Beijing, Central Bank of Nigeria @cenbank Governor Olayemi Cardoso (@olayemicardoso1) led discussions across two major forums aimed at expanding Nigeria’s economic and financial ties with China.\n\nThe first gathering brought together business executives, financial experts and industry stakeholders operating along the Nigeria–China trade corridor. Conversations centred on payment systems, foreign exchange, trade financing and the challenges businesses face when conducting cross-border transactions.\n\nThe second forum, organised in collaboration with ICBC, focused on investment opportunities within Nigeria’s financial markets. Institutional investors, development finance organisations and other market participants examined ways to encourage investment and create a more supportive environment for capital inflows.\n\nCardoso also highlighted the importance of improving remittance services for Nigerians living abroad. The CBN’s focus includes making international transfers more affordable, accessible and efficient, while strengthening the financial links between the diaspora and Nigeria’s domestic economy.\n\nRead More 👇\nhttps://t.co/yy1mTATnKV…\n\n@Dattijo",
